            <div xml:id="d923">

                <pb facs="1050" n="957" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg957"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">633.113/17</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 140</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-12-27">December 27, 1935</date>.<lb/>[Received January 4,
                        1936.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Department’s Instructions No.
                    11 of July 22, 1935, No. 17 of August 13, 1935 and No. 22 of September 10,
                        1935,<anchor n="9" xml:id="d923-f1"/> and Despatches from the Legation Nos.
                    65 and 66 of August 23, 1935, No. 85 of September 10, 1935 and No. 94 of October
                    1, 1935,<anchor n="10" xml:id="d923-f2"/> regarding discriminatory customs
                    treatment of imports of American lumber and other products, I have the honor to
                    enclose herewith copy and translation of a note from the Uruguayan Foreign
                    Office of December 23, 1935, in reply to mine of August 10, 1935<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d923-f3"/> (transmitted to the Department with Despatch No. 94 of
                    October 1, 1935) from which it appears that the discriminatory customs treatment
                    of lumber and a number of other commodities, complained of in my note, is to be
                    removed.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julius G. Lay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
